BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/painting-flora-and-fauna/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Painting Flora and Fauna in Watercolor
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T130000
UID:260211xRcxNzo2_U-UUrFEbZ7-NA
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nFridays\, March. 20- April 24\, 2026 10:00 AM – 
 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nDrawi
 ng & Painting\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\n$275 – Registration Cost 
 $25 – Materials Fee $300 – Total Registration CostIn this six-week cou
 rse\, participants will learn a unique approach to watercolor\, intended t
 o alleviate the frustration that many experience when learning this beauti
 ful yet challenging medium.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nIn this six-week course\
 , participants will learn a unique approach to watercolor\, intended to al
 leviate the frustration that many experience when learning this beautiful 
 yet challenging medium. We will focus on strengthening one’s observation
 al drawing skills\, giving the artist a foundation off of which to build t
 heir paintings in a step-by-step layering process that trains the artist t
 o see value and color. Our subject matter will be flora and fauna – a sa
 mpling of plants and animals. These subjects are great for beginners and e
 xperienced artists alike\; their organic shapes make them forgiving drawin
 g subjects\, but their beauty can be a muse for life.  Instructor Hannah 
 Day is a passionate nature lover and watercolorist and will share her uniq
 ue approach to rendering botanicals and animal portraits in watercolor. Th
 is class will work both from photographs and from life\, practicing observ
 ational drawing in addition to watercolor technique. With six class sessio
 ns\, participants will have the opportunity to develop their skills and bu
 ild muscle memory with a medium that often feels like it has a mind of its
  own.  This class is open to artists of all skill levels. All materials a
 re provided.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/painting-flora-and-fauna/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.sebastopolgallery.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Journey: A Painter's Narrative
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T170000
UID:2601286sOWKotnak-bkg7l3Oe5iw
DESCRIPTION:New Woman and Fox paintings by Teri Sloat celebrate the person
 al journeys we take as we travel outward through landscape trails or inwar
 d through thoughts and dreams. Her ongoing series\, Woman and Fox\, A Jour
 ney\, present rich\, metaphorical paintings that invite you to pause on yo
 ur own path and enjoy the distance you have come.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:https://www.sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/", "Press Democrat": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Bonsai Show: Bonsai & Blossoms
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T170000
UID:260108rCNuic7QCkuQyegim9yI-Q
DESCRIPTION:January 9–March 22\, 2026\n\nStep into a wonderland of bloom
 ing miniature trees to marvel at the living art of bonsai and the season
 ’s first flowers. Then stroll through our Asian Woodland to admire maje
 stic magnolias\, cherries\, and camellias in bloom\, or join a tour or pro
 gram to explore this timeless craft.\n\nThis year’s all-new presentation
  by the skilled artisans of the Redwood Empire Bonsai Society \\(REBS\\) h
 ighlights the grace and vitality of flowering bonsai—trees and shrubs tr
 ained to bloom in exquisite proportion to their diminutive scale. Delicate
  plum\, azalea\, camellia\, cherry\, and apricot bonsai take center stag
 e\, their blossoms appearing just as winter begins to yield to spring. The
 se early bloomers symbolize hope and renewal—reminding us that beauty an
 d resilience can emerge even in the coldest months.\n\nThe exhibition also
  draws inspiration from hanami\, the centuries-old Japanese tradition of 
 celebrating the fleeting beauty of blossoms. The Garden invites visitors t
 o participate in this art of flower appreciation through Hanami Strolls
 —guided walks through the Garden’s Asian woodland where early-blooming
  magnolias\, cherries\, and camellias offer their own ephemeral display.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/bonsai-and-blossoms/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
