X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/a-night-with-national-geographic-urban-ecologist-dr-chris-schell/18137923/2026-03-20T18", "Press Democrat": "https://mynorthbaytickets.com/e/napa-center-for-thought-culture-presents-chris-sch/tickets"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/a-night-with-national-geographic-urban-ecologist-dr-chris-schell/18137923/2026-03-20T18"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:A Night with National Geographic Urban Ecologist Dr. Chris Schell
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T180000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T193000
UID:260217XQJEtMiARk-IVwScExfWNA
DESCRIPTION:A Night with National Geographic Urban Ecologist Dr. Chris Sch
 ell\n\nFriday\, March 20\n\nEcoLab Theater at CIA Copia\, Napa CA\n\nDoors
 : 5:30 PM | Program 6:00 PM\n\nThink wildlife lives “somewhere else”? 
 Think again. Join National Geographic Explorer Dr. Chris Schell for a mind
 -expanding journey into the surprising world of urban coyotes\, foxes\, ra
 ccoons — and the hidden histories that shaped the ecosystems right outsi
 de our doors.\n\nDr. Schell’s groundbreaking work uncovers how environme
 ntal injustice\, resilience\, and human choices ripple through entire citi
 es\, transforming the animals who live alongside us. You’ll never see a 
 neighborhood stroll the same way again.\n\nA powerful\, eye-opening evenin
 g for anyone curious about science\, justice\, and the wild stories unfold
 ing in our own backyard.\n\nBe curious.  Be surprised.  Be there.
LOCATION:CIA at Copia
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/a-night-with-national-g
 eographic-urban-ecologist-dr-chris-schell/18137923/2026-03-20T18
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/napa-center-for-thought-culture-presents-chris-sch?aff=cityspark", "Press Democrat": "https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/napa-center-for-thought-culture-presents-chris-sch?aff=cityspark"}
