BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/the-glass-menagerie-by-tennessee-williams/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Glass Menagerie
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T213000
UID:2602279BqdwhEDbE-S_XHR6w7LYg
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 Season at Curtain Call Theatre starts off with **The 
 Glass Menagerie**\, the play that made Tennessee Williams famous.\n\nHave 
 You Ever Felt Stuck Between Your Dreams and Reality? This Play Gets It.\n\
 nImagine being trapped in a tiny apartment during the Great Depression —
  no money\, no way out\, just a family clinging to hopes that may never co
 me true. That's exactly what The Glass Menagerie is about.\n\nWritten by T
 ennessee Williams — one of America's greatest playwrights — this story
  follows a restless son\, an overbearing mom\, and a painfully shy daughte
 r as they each chase dreams that feel just out of reach. It's emotional\, 
 poetic\, and honestly… kind of hits different when you think about your 
 own life.\n\nThis iconic play is literally studied in classrooms worldwide
 \, so seeing it live is like watching your textbook come to life — excep
 t way more powerful.\n\n📅 March 13–29\, 2026\n\n📍 20347 Hwy 116\, 
 Monte Rio\, CA\n\n🎟️ Grab your tickets at russianriverhall.com or cal
 l (707) 387-5072\n\nThe Glass Menagerie by Tennessee Williams is directed 
 by Michael Tabib.\n\nShowing at the Russian River Hall in Monte Rio\, CA f
 rom March 13-29\, 2026.\n\nProgram was made possible\, in part\, with fund
 s from Creative Sonoma and the California Arts Council (CAC).\n\nBy specia
 l arrangement with Dramatists Play Services\, Inc.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-mena
 gerie/
X-SOURCE:Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/marjorie-prime/", "GoLocal Cooperative": "https://golocal.coop/event/marjorie-prime-at-6th-street-playhouse-7/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/marjorie-prime/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Marjorie Prime
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260320T205000
UID:250801WLRqtKEvJU661ZILrSZtrg
DESCRIPTION:**Artificial Remembrance: The Intersection of Technology and M
 emory**\n\n***“Jordan Harrison’s gently uncanny play imagines a future
  solution for a person in mourning: the recreation of someone you love as 
 an artificial intelligence.”* —Kate Wyver\, The Guardian**\n\n**In *Ma
 rjorie Prime*\, playwright Jordan Harrison delves into the intricate dance
  between human memory and artificial intelligence. Set in the not-so-dista
 nt future\, the narrative centers on 85-year-old Marjorie\, whose mind is 
 gradually succumbing to dementia. To combat her fading recollections\, her
  family introduces her to a “Prime”—a lifelike holographic projectio
 n of her late husband\, Walter\, programmed to retell the stories of their
  shared past. As Marjorie interacts with Walter Prime\, the lines between 
 authentic memories and reconstructed narratives blur\, prompting profound 
 questions about identity\, the reliability of our recollections\, and the 
 extent to which technology can replicate the essence of human connection. 
 This thought-provoking drama challenges audiences to consider what we choo
 se to remember\, what we wish to forget\, and how the digital age reshapes
  the very fabric of our personal histories.**\n\n***Marjorie Prime* has ga
 rnered critical acclaim for its insightful exploration and profound commen
 tary on the human condition in an era where technology increasingly intert
 wines with our daily lives.**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays & Saturdays @ 7:30pm\
 , Saturdays and Sundays at 2:00pm Run Time: One hour\, 20 mins including i
 ntermission\n\nThursdays Adult $33 Fri/Sat Eve Adult $39.95\; Senior $36.9
 5\; Under 18 $26.95 Sat/Sun Matinee Adult $47.95\; Senior $44.95 \\*All pr
 ices include fees (707) 523-4185 **boxoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/marjorie-prime/
X-SOURCE:GoLocal Cooperative, North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
