BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/identity-and-its-discontents-with-kendell-pinkney/18281953/2026-03-21T16"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Identity and its Discontents with Kendell Pinkney
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T160000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T173000
UID:260311f3AiRaImjUuc4dUxjjwsTA
DESCRIPTION:To live as a Black Jew in North America is to live with a keen
  awareness of just how precarious group belonging can be\, yet a felt sens
 e of ‘belonging’ is a core human need. Between this self-evident need 
 for community and the complexities of contemporary identity\, lies a uniqu
 e space bounded by subtle challenges and creative possibilities. Join thea
 tre artist and rabbi\, Kendell Pinkney\, for an evening of conversation\, 
 experimentation\, and excerpts from his theatre work that probes the bound
 aries of Black\, Jewish\, and rabbinic identity.\n\nKendell Pinkney is a N
 ew York based playwright\, librettist\, and rabbi. His collaborative theat
 re works have been presented at venues such as Feinstein’s 54 Below\, Jo
 e’s Pub\, LABA @ the 14th St. Y\, and Two River Theatre\, to name a few.
  Recent play commissions include I Know of Plagues for Theater J and Dougl
 ass in Britannia for RedYes Studio. As a rabbi\, he has been featured in t
 he acclaimed docuseries "The New Jew\," with actor-comedian Guri Alfi\, Bu
 zzFeed’s Tasty channel broadcast of “Saturday Night Seder\,” and Cro
 oked Media’s religion and society podcast\, “Unholier than Thou.”\n\
 nKendell currently serves as the Director of Jewish Learning at Reboot\, 
 and is the founding Artistic Director of The Workshop \\(theworkshopny.com
  / @theworkshopartist\\) - a New York based arts and culture fellowship t
 hat supports and foregrounds the work of professional artists of BIPOC-Jew
 ish heritage.
LOCATION:Congregation Rodef Sholom
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/identity-and-its-discon
 tents-with-kendell-pinkney/18281953/2026-03-21T16
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/products/mary-blair-mid-century-modern-opening-celebration", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/mary-blair-mid-century-magic-opening-celebration/18285242/2026-03-21T16"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/products/mary-blair-mid-century-modern-opening-celebration"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Mary Blair: Mid-Century Magic Opening Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T160000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T190000
UID:260311BrvChrgLfE-rMqo2PhqiPQ
DESCRIPTION:The **Napa Valley Museum Yountville (NVMY)** invites you to
  step into a world of imagination and color as we celebrate the opening of
  **“*Mary Blair: Mid-Century Magic”*** on March 21\, 2026 —a specia
 l exhibition created by the Walt Disney Family Museum. Co-hosted by **NVM
 Y\, the Walt Disney Family Museum\, and Tiki Oasis**\, this opening celebr
 ation offers guests a first look into Mary Blair’s iconic playful palett
 es and whimsical spirit she brought to some of Disney’s most beloved mov
 ies.\n\nThroughout the evening\, delightful surprises will unfold\, includ
 ing a 60's inspired dance performance by **The** **Devil-Ettes\,** mid-c
 entury music by our resident DJ**\,** cocktails by **Hanson of Sonoma Dis
 tillery\,** and small bites by **Sushi Monkey.** Guests are encouraged
  to attend in **cocktail attire or mid-century 50s–60s style**. \n\n*
 *4 p.m. First Look for Priority Access\, Museum Member & MAC Pack** incl
 udes signature cocktail created by Hanson of Sonoma Distillery and gift fr
 om the NVMY\n\n**5-7 p.m. General Admission**: Celebration continues with
  cocktails\, sushi and music.\n\n*Join us as we toast to imagination and t
 he radiant legacy of Mary Blair.*
LOCATION:Napa Valley Museum Yountville
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/products/mary-blair-mid-century-modern-op
 ening-celebration
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
