UID:260218vdjqUGMTwEOK2-INVs6Yag
DESCRIPTION:Mercy Presents: Puff N’ Paint – Glow In The Dark Edition S
 aturday\, March 21\, 2026 | 7:00 PM – 10:00 PM 📍 The Lounge at Mercy\
 n\nTap into your creative flow at Mercy’s Glow-In-The-Dark Puff N’ Pai
 nt—a high-vibe\, black light–lit art experience where cannabis culture
 \, creativity\, and community collide inside The Lounge at Mercy.\n\nThis 
 isn’t your average paint night. Under immersive black lights\, neon and 
 glow-in-the-dark paints come alive as you sip\, puff\, and create in a rel
 axed\, visually electric atmosphere designed to spark imagination and conn
 ection. Whether you’re dialed into your canvas or vibing with the room\,
  this session is all about expression\, conversation\, and good energy—n
 o pressure\, just pure creative fun.\n\nGuided by smooth evening beats\, w
 atch your artwork transform as the lights go low and the glow turns on. Ex
 pect trippy colors\, luminous strokes\, and a one-of-a-kind masterpiece yo
 u’ll take home at the end of the night.\n\nPresented by Emerald Sky and 
 Papa’s Herb\, this immersive experience is your invitation to slow down\
 , light up\, and let your creativity glow—Mercy style.\n\n🎨 What’s 
 Included:\n\n- All glow-in-the-dark and neon painting supplies\n\n- Black 
 light–powered Puff N’ Paint experience\n\n- Zero-pressure creative ses
 sion\n\n- Take-home canvas masterpiece\n\n- Atmosphere buzzing with smooth
  evening beats\n\n- Cannabis-friendly lounge to spark creativity\n\n🎟 T
 icket Tiers:\n\nLimited to 80 guests\n\nGeneral Admission – $35 Includes
  paint supplies only\n\nVIP Tier 1 – $50 Includes $25 Goodie Bag\n\nVIP 
 Tier 2 – $75 Includes $50 Goodie Bag\n\n✨ Come for the glow. Stay for 
 the vibe. Leave with art that lights up the night.\n\n21\\+ Only | DCC \\#
  C12-0000420-LIC
LOCATION:The Lounge at Mercy
URL:https://www.themercylounge.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sgvperformingarts.eventcalendarapp.com/jerome-rubin-and-friends"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Jerome Rubin and Friends : the If Not Now Fugghedaboutit Tour Retu
 rns
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T190000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T210000
UID:260212YI7ks4Kfs0CCAiRQQIzvvQ
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday March 21\, 2026 at 7pm\, the San Geronimo Valley 
 Community Center welcomes back Jerome Rubin and Friends AND the return o
 f the “If Not Now Fuhgeddaboutit Tour.” This time Jerome's bringing 
 some friends including\, Bruce Friedberg - electric accordion\, ukulele\,
  vocals\, Anthony Parber - Bass\, vocals\, Doug Martin - Lap Steel Guitar\
 , Dobro and Brad Elias - Percussion\, vocals.\n\nSince we last saw Jerome 
 play the Community Center in 2024\, he took the INNF Tour overseas. Last s
 ummer Jerome travelled all over Europe for three months of reconnecting wi
 th friends\, and successful music gatherings\, open mics and concerts in t
 he Maritimes Alpes in the south of France\, Berlin and other cities in Ger
 many\; Krakow\, Poland\, Prague\, Czech Republic\, and Strasbourg\, France
 . His return to Europe marked 50 years since he had first moved to Europe 
 in 1975 and lived for seven years.\n\nJerome Rubin has been singing since 
 birth and has performed in hundreds of concerts throughout Europe and the 
 United States. He is well known for his emotive singing voice and heartfel
 t interpretations of Bob Dylan\, Van Morrison\, Tom Waits\, American stand
 ards and many others. Jerome’s original songs and stories have won award
 s\, touched and inspired many.\n\nAnyone who saw Jerome and this band at K
 ate’s Cafe in November 2025 knows this is a show not to be missed!
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sgvperformingarts.eventcalendarapp.com/jerome-rubin-and-friend
 s
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
