X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/santa-rosa-symphony-rossini-schubert/", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/santa-rosa-symphony-rossini-schubert/", "Press Democrat": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/santa-rosa-symphony-rossini-schubert/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/santa-rosa-symphony-rossini-schubert/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Santa Rosa Symphony - Rossini & Schubert
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T203000
UID:260312Vl7nHUEqSEWUz2Oyy6a02w
DESCRIPTION:Rossini & Schubert March 21\, 22 & 23\, 2026 Weill Hall\, Gree
 n Music Center Francesco Lecce-Chong\, conductor Elizabeth Prior\, viola A
 delle-Akiko Kearns\, cello Roy Zajac\, clarinet Robert Giambruno\, trumpet
  Bruce Chrisp\, trombone Allen Biggs\, marimba GIOACHINO ROSSINI: Overture
  to Il barberiere di Siviglia \\[The Barber of Seville\\] SHUYING LI: Copi
 ng Cadences \\(World Premiere\\) FRANZ SCHUBERT: Symphony No. 8 in B minor
 \, D.759\, Unfinished GIOACHINO ROSSINI: Overture to Guillaume Tell \\[Wil
 liam Tell\\] Celebrate the artistry of two musical giants: Rossini's spark
 ling wit and Schubert's moving melodies. With its theatrical flair and rhy
 thm-driven energy\, Rossini's William Tell Overture contrasts beautifully 
 with Schubert's Unfinished Symphony\, which offers a glimpse of his profou
 nd creative brilliance and introspective lyricism. Additionally\, the worl
 d premiere of Shuying Li's concerto grosso Coping Cadences ignites the ima
 gination while merging traditional and contemporary elements. Programs\, d
 ates\, artists\, and prices are subject to change without notice. Tickets 
 are nonrefundable and subject to availability.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/santa-rosa-symphony-rossini-schubert/
X-SOURCE:Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Glass Menagerie
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T213000
UID:260227WFCqFyCUbEyiBIKF9eNBmA
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 Season at Curtain Call Theatre starts off with **The 
 Glass Menagerie**\, the play that made Tennessee Williams famous.\n\nHave 
 You Ever Felt Stuck Between Your Dreams and Reality? This Play Gets It.\n\
 nImagine being trapped in a tiny apartment during the Great Depression —
  no money\, no way out\, just a family clinging to hopes that may never co
 me true. That's exactly what The Glass Menagerie is about.\n\nWritten by T
 ennessee Williams — one of America's greatest playwrights — this story
  follows a restless son\, an overbearing mom\, and a painfully shy daughte
 r as they each chase dreams that feel just out of reach. It's emotional\, 
 poetic\, and honestly… kind of hits different when you think about your 
 own life.\n\nThis iconic play is literally studied in classrooms worldwide
 \, so seeing it live is like watching your textbook come to life — excep
 t way more powerful.\n\n📅 March 13–29\, 2026\n\n📍 20347 Hwy 116\, 
 Monte Rio\, CA\n\n🎟️ Grab your tickets at russianriverhall.com or cal
 l (707) 387-5072\n\nThe Glass Menagerie by Tennessee Williams is directed 
 by Michael Tabib.\n\nShowing at the Russian River Hall in Monte Rio\, CA f
 rom March 13-29\, 2026.\n\nProgram was made possible\, in part\, with fund
 s from Creative Sonoma and the California Arts Council (CAC).\n\nBy specia
 l arrangement with Dramatists Play Services\, Inc.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-mena
 gerie/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
