BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup: Go Wild Hikers": "https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-go-wild-hikers/events/313686476/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_go_wild_hikers
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Go Wild Hikers
UID:event_313686476@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260318T052421Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260322T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260322T120000
SUMMARY:Re-scheduled Lake Sonoma Hike
DESCRIPTION:Go Wild Hikers\nWildflowers are early this year\, and I have already seen some Orchids. Join me in search of early wildflowers at Lake Sonoma. We'll hike through a magical madrone forest\, take in beautiful expansive views of the Mayacamas Mountain range as well as the Dry Creek and Warm Springs arms of Lake Sonoma. We will visit some of the largest manzanita and madrone trees I've seen. Best for individuals and dogs with at least a moderate level of fitness.\n\n**Where We Meet/Important Directions**\nLittle Flat Parking (A large gravel parking lot)\nFrom Hwy 101 take Dry Creek Road west towards Lake Sonoma. Go up the hill and across the bridge over the lake. Pay Attention\, it's the first right turn into "Little Flat" parking lot.\nGive yourself plenty of time to arrive. It's often farther than you think.\n\n**Group Hike #336**\nDry Creek\, No Name\, North Slope and Bummer trails - a loop hike\nLength - +/-5 miles/8 kilometers\nElevation change - +/-900 feet/274 meters\nDifficulty - 7+ out of 10 some short steep rocky sections\nMust be sure footed (confident and competent)!\nExposures - +/-30 % sun/70% shade - creek crossings\, rocky\, muddy\, poison oak\, ticks/insects.\nBring plenty of water. At least 68 oz./2 liters!\nDogs - Yes\, must be healthy\, well behaved and on a leash.\nFacilities at trail head - None - Port O Potti about 1.5 miles in.\nCost - $5 cash\nParking -$7-day pass can be purchased on-site using a credit card through the Recreation.gov mobile app. Once on-site\, follow the posted Scan & Pay instructions. You will need to download the free Recreation.gov mobile app prior to your arrival as some remote areas have limited or no cellular service. For more information about paying on-site\, click here: [How Do I Use a Scan & Pay QR Code to Purchase an Activity Pass?](https://recreationonestoptest.servicenowservices.com/external?id=kb_article&sys_id=2011ea4a1b84bcd076c1dbdbe54bcb1d)\nRemember to wear appropriate hiking shoes\, bring plenty of water for your dog too\, a hat\, snack\, layered clothing.\nPlease Do Not Use Any scented products the day of a group hike!\nOf course\, we will all look out for each other but ultimately\, hikers are responsible for their own safety and well-being during hikes.\n\n**After Hike Gathering?**\nQuail & Condor\nBakery and Café\n44 Mill St Unit J\nHealdsburg\, CA 95448\n[https://www.quailandcondor.com/](https://www.quailandcondor.com/)\n(707) 473-8254\nOutstanding new location with plenty of parking and a beautiful cafe. Behind the Parish Café at the roundabout.\n\n**When We Meet**\nSunday March 22\, 2026\n9:00 am - 12:00 pm\nIf your plans change after you sign up even if you're on the waitlist\, please update your RSVP.\nDo Not Attend if you are sick\, running a fever\, were exposed to or have tested positive for Covid-19 or any other contagion!\nHike may be changed\, rescheduled or cancelled in case of excessive heat\, rain\, smoke/AQI\, illness\, zombie apocalypse etc... Check your email the night before for any possible changes.\n\n**Notice to New Hikers Only**\n**"When a New Hiker (never hiked with me before) doesn't show up (No Show) to their first hike with the group\, they will be removed (not banned) from the group immediately."**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-go-wild-hikers/events/313686476/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260307T215118Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260307T215118Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/7/1/c/600_500230012.jpeg
END:VEVENT
