X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.cedarslife.org/events"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:"You're My Neighbor" Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260322T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260322T170000
UID:260227igSKjzg7YUS8ZxzWePSRNA
DESCRIPTION:Come out to Point Reyes and celebrate neighbors!   \n\nFrom 
 mooing cows and soaring birds to friendly faces down the road\, Cedars art
 ists take a joyful look at their Marin County neighborhood. This exhibitio
 n explores all the things that make their corner of the world special—op
 en fields\, wild creatures\, familiar people\, and the everyday moments in
  between. Through colorful\, thoughtful\, and imaginative works\, “You
 ’re My Neighbor” celebrates the beauty of living side by side and shar
 ing a place we call home.\n\n​Cedars “You’re My Neighbor!” art exh
 ibition runs from March 3 through April 12\, 2026
LOCATION:Toby's Feed Barn
URL:https://www.cedarslife.org/events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/japanese-papermaking/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Japanese Papermaking
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260322T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260322T160000
UID:260216Grnh-kLzhkajiBEsu2zc-Q
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, March 21\, 2026 2:00 PM – 5:00 PM Sun
 day\, March 22\, 2026 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nExpe
 rience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nBilingual\, Fiber Arts\, Printmaking\n\nAge\
 \(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\n$180 – Registration Cost $25 – Materials Fee
  $205 – Total Registration CostLearn traditional Japanese papermaking us
 ing the nagashizuki method. Beat fiber by hand and form delicate\, strong 
 sheets to take home. All levels welcome.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nIn this wor
 kshop\, students will be introduced to the process of making Japanese pape
 r. Japanese paper\, often incorrectly referred to as rice paper\, is known
  for its great strength while appearing delicate and gossamer-thin. In thi
 s workshop\, students will learn the basics of preparing their own fiber\,
  hand beating\, and forming sheets in the traditional nagashizuki method. 
 Students will take home wet sheets to dry at home with instructions. Pleas
 e be aware that papermaking is a wet activity –  wear clothing and shoe
 s that can get wet. Class involves some physical activity\, including stan
 ding and arm movements. All supplies are provided through the materials fe
 e. La maestra habla español. Note: Please bring a bag lunch on Sunday.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/japanese-papermaking/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/reclaiming-who-we-are-with-self-compassion-kn1m26/?lang=en", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/reclaiming-who-we-are-with-self-compassion/18115202/2026-03-22T10"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/reclaiming-who-we-are-with-self-compassion-kn1m26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Reclaiming Who We Are with Self-Compassion
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260322T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260322T163000
UID:260214CkI4DkAPPUufXzGfAZMK9g
DESCRIPTION:with Kristin Neff\, PhD and Caverly Morgan\n\nSelf-compassion 
 helps us let go of identification with the belief that we’re not good en
 ough. With its warm support\, we learn to untangle from our negative thoug
 hts and emotions and embrace our inherent wholeness.\n\nOur unconscious co
 nditioning—influenced by our family\, genetics\, and culture—often tel
 ls us we’re inadequate and need to be different in order to be happy. Co
 mpassion helps us remember who we truly are versus who we’ve been condit
 ioned to be. It transforms our contracted and limited view of ourselves\, 
 opening to a larger\, more connected\, and powerful sense of loving presen
 ce.\n\nResearch shows that self-compassion is strongly linked to psycholog
 ical and physical health\, but our conditioning works against being kind t
 o ourselves. In this program\, researcher Kristin Neff teams up with medit
 ation teacher Caverly Morgan to explore self-compassion from a scientific 
 and contemplative lens\, so that we can respond to difficult moments with 
 greater warmth and perspective.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/reclaiming-who-we-are-
 with-self-compassion-kn1m26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.sebastopolgallery.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
