BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://app.gohighlevel.com/v2/preview/YBevNs5UaOhr3dVfig7Q"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Aging Well with Intention: Caregivers & Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T110000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T123000
UID:260317HwfEhFSO0023KWFgE_XIzQ
DESCRIPTION:The Aging Well with Intention Blueprint introduces a person-
 centered planning framework designed to help seniors and family caregivers
  plan ahead before a crisis occurs. This presentation addresses common g
 aps in planning and communication\, offering practical insights to reduce 
 overwhelm\, support smoother transitions\, and improve long-term outcomes 
 for aging adults and their families. \n\nWho should attend:  \n\nSenior
 s who want to plan ahead and stay in control of their future \n\nAdult 
 children supporting aging parents \n\nFamilies who want clarity before de
 cisions become urgent \n\nCaregivers looking for structure and guidance 
 \n\nAnyone who prefers proactive planning over crisis management \n\n Wh
 at you will learn:  \n\nHow to plan ahead instead of reacting in a cri
 sis \n\nThe common mistakes families make when they wait too long \n\nHo
 w to navigate housing\, care options\, and transitions \n\nWays to reduce
  stress and protect independence \n\nHow to create a clear direction for 
 the next chapter \n\n Workshop benefits:  \n\nGet clear on what you wa
 nt your future to look like \n\nUnderstand decisions now — before they 
 become urgent \n\nCreate a practical plan for your health\, lifestyle\, a
 nd legacy \n\nReduce stress by having structure and direction \n\nFeel m
 ore confident discussing next steps with family \n\n This is a practical
 \, no-pressure workshop focused on the real transitions that come with agi
 ng — housing decisions\, changing health needs\, and the family conversa
 tions that are easier to have before urgency takes over. \n\nThis isn’
 t a legal seminar. \n\nIt’s about getting clear\, protecting your ind
 ependence\, and making thoughtful decisions while you still have the time 
 and space to choose.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing Finley Community Center
URL:https://app.gohighlevel.com/v2/preview/YBevNs5UaOhr3dVfig7Q
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/author-talks-americas-failed-response-opioid-crisis-shoshana-walter-104479"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:America's Failed Response to the Opioid Crisis with Shoshana Walte
 r
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T110000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T120000
UID:2603123ncPPz4TnU2ZKw3OayOGXA
DESCRIPTION:America's Failed Response to the Opioid Crisis with Shoshana W
 alter With Special Guest Host Barbara Kingsolver Register here: Join us fo
 r a special conversation between award-winning journalist Shoshana Walter 
 and bestselling and award-winning author Barbara Kingsolver as they chat a
 bout Walter's book Rehab: An American Scandal. In this work\, Walter\, a P
 ulitzer finalist\, exposes the country's failed response to the opioid cri
 sis\, and the malfeasance\, corruption\, and snake oil which blight the dr
 ug rehabilitation industry. About the Author: Shoshana Walter is a reporte
 r for the Marshall Project covering the criminal justice system. Her repor
 ting has been honored as a finalist for the Pulitzer Prize and Selden Ring
 \, and she has won the Knight Award for Public Service\, the Edward R. Mur
 row Award\, and the Livingston Award for Young Journalists. She started he
 r work on the treatment system at The Center for Investigative Reporting\,
  where her work appeared in The New York Times Magazine\, in newspapers\, 
 and on NPR stations across the country. She is based in Oakland\, Californ
 ia. About the Guest Host: Barbara Ellen Kingsolver is a Pulitzer Prize-win
 ning American novelist\, essayist\, and poet. Her widely known works inclu
 de The Poisonwood Bible\, the tale of a missionary family in the Congo\, a
 nd Animal\, Vegetable\, Miracle\, a nonfiction account of her family's att
 empts to eat locally. In 2023\, she was awarded the Pulitzer Prize for Fic
 tion for the novel Demon Copperhead. Her work often focuses on topics such
  as social justice\, biodiversity\, and the interaction between humans and
  their communities and environments.
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/author-talks-americas-failed-re
 sponse-opioid-crisis-shoshana-walter-104479
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net", "Press Democrat": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Celebrating Women
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T110000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260324T180000
UID:260217Ly7dCvW-1EeImaUqKF_VcA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  2/13/26\n\n**MARCH EXHIBIT: CELE
 BRATING WOMEN**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  February 23 – March 29\, 2026\n\n**R
 ECEPTION: SATURDAY\, MARCH 7\, 2026\, 4-6 pm: Join in to meet the artists 
 and celebrate the show. Take part in the Gallery’s free monthly drawing 
 for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**
 \n\nSonoma County artist\, **Tosya Shore\,** presents **Celebrating Women\
 ,** paintings that commemorate women in honor of Women’s History Month. 
 Shore’s watercolor works capture women in their element\, showing the mu
 ltiple facets of their lives.  These dynamic paintings break away with st
 rong shapes and interlacing patterns that draw the viewer in exciting ways
 .  A la Degas\, we catch a ballet dancer lacing her shoes in “Good Poin
 t.”  The artist takes us into nature with “Redwood Rendezvous” wher
 e dominant trunk shapes frame a couple enjoying a glorious forest scene. 
    “Just Back from Vegas” captures a fleeting view of elegance as th
 e woman in question catches her breath.  “There’s such special feelin
 g in these everyday moments\, I love to turn the mundane into magic – wo
 men deserve nothing less\,” noted Shore. \n\nMeet the artist: Shore wil
 l be hosting the Gallery on March 5 and 19 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n The Sta
 irway Smallworks Showcase features **Donna Schaffer’s Ooh La La\, Plein 
 Air\,** a collection unveiling oil paintings made on her recent trip to Fr
 ance.  Roaming the streets of Paris\, toting paints and palette\, Schaffe
 r captured iconic scenes buzzing with “la belle vie.” The viewer catch
 es a true cultural vibe in “Café le Bistro”\, the site of a favored h
 angout for espresso and conversation.  One is awed by the structure risin
 g from the ground-level trees in Schaffer’s unique view of the Eiffel To
 wer in “Paris is for Lovers.” “Every day was an adventure in Paris 
 – I hope through these plein air vignettes\, to share the excitement of 
 being there”\, stated Schaffer.\n\nMeet the artist: Schaffer will be hos
 ting the Gallery on March 21 and 22 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nUpstairs Art Gal
 lery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DA
 ILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further 
 information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net o
 r 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
