BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/distant-voices-an-introduction-to-asemic-writing"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Distant Voices: An Introduction to Asemic Writing — Sebastopol C
 enter For the Arts\, California
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T000000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T000000
UID:cbfa7af3099b1575974decb15b5ac1f1@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Distant Voices: An Introduction to Asemic Writing\n\n  \n    \
 n      \n        \n          $165.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSaturd
 ay\, March 28\, 2026\; 10am - 4pm$150 + $15 materials feeAsemic writing is
  the practice of creating artwork through marks that resemble handwriting\
 , yet carry no literal meaning or readable text. It is the word before wor
 ds form—the voice too distant to be understood—a cosmic expression wit
 hout country or dialect.We’ll begin with a slideshow exploring the depth
  and range of asemic writing. Looking at ancient scripts\, global language
 s\, symbols\, the calligraphic line\, and the work of contemporary asemic 
 artists\, we’ll expand our understanding of what is possible.From there\
 , you’ll begin your own asemic journey. These marks can infiltrate and t
 ransform your current artwork\, or stand alone as independent works of art
 .IMPORTANT: View supplies list in the attached PDF.  Using ink and waterco
 lor with a variety of tools\, we’ll explore how to express what does not
  need to be said in words. My intention is to guide you toward authentic m
 arks—marks that arise from the heart and move beyond casual scribbling i
 nto something deeply felt and uniquely your own. All levels welcome.About 
 the Instructor: Sherrie Lovler holds a BA in Studio Art and has been teach
 ing calligraphy and related arts for several decades. Well-known in the We
 stern calligraphy community\, she has taught at international calligraphy 
 conferences as well as at Ghost Ranch\, Friends of Calligraphy in San Fran
 cisco\, Society of Scribes in NYC\, La Romita School of Art in Italy\, Nor
 thern Arizona University\, O’Hanlon Center for the Arts\, and Sebastopol
  Center for the Arts. She is the author\, illustrator\, and designer of "O
 n Softer Ground: Paintings\, Poems and Calligraphy"\, which received a Gol
 d Medal for Most Outstanding Book Design from the Independent Publisher Bo
 ok Awards. Her newest book\, "Distant Voices\," features 31 full-color pai
 ntings and nine poems\, accompanied by an introduction exploring her thoug
 hts and creative process Sherrie exhibits her work in juried shows\, solo 
 exhibitions\, Art Trails and Art at the Source open studios in Sonoma Coun
 ty. She enjoys teaching both online and in person. www.artandpoetry.com\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        \n 
          \n            \n              Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/distant-voices-an-introductio
 n-to-asemic-writing
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/explore-gel-plate-printing"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Explore Gel Plate Printing — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, Ca
 lifornia
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T000000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T000000
UID:27330496c0eb50ab741419f0a224c01a@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Explore Gel Plate Printing\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n    
       $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, March 28\, 2026\; 
 11 AM – 3 PMFee: $115 + $15 materials feeAge: 16+ Participants: min. 8Le
 arn to create beautiful designs on paper by printing with a gel plate and 
 acrylic paint. Mixed media artist Catherine Cruz will teach you the basic 
 skills for using this fun tool from printing textural backgrounds\, to lay
 ering colors\, and using stencils and other applications. You will take ho
 me many prints that can be used for designing collage\, mixed media art or
  greeting cards. This class is suitable for anyone wanting to learn this u
 nique mono printing style and perfect for beginners.What you’ll get from
  this workshop: Methods for applying paint and pulling successful prints (
 Note: Magazine image transfer is not included in this class.)\, Techniques
  for creating intricate layered designs\, Creative use of mark-making tool
 s and masks\, Strategies for combining techniques.A variety of papers will
  be provided but you are highly encouraged to bring your own papers to exp
 eriment on.IMPORTANT: Instructions for where to purchase your materials an
 d how to prepare them is provided in the attached PDF. The instructor will
  start the class with a demonstration so please arrive a few minutes early
  to get set up so we can start on time.  We will take a short break for lu
 nch between 12:30 and 1:00 pm so bring your lunch and a beverage.  About t
 he instructor: Catherine Cruz is a French-American artist whose work is in
 formed by textures and patterns created by the passing of time and the eff
 ects of the natural elements on the built environment.  She holds a Bachel
 or of Science in interior design and she worked in the field of architectu
 ral design and green building certification for over 25 years.  She has ta
 ught collage and mixed media workshops in the Bay Area and in France since
  2019\, and this is her fifth year at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts. 
  Her studio is located in Sebastopol and she participates in Art Trails Op
 en Studios.  You may contact Catherine at beyouartstudio@gmail.com.  Check
  out Catherine’s other classes here:  https://wwws.sebarts.org/visual-ar
 ts-classes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n        \n          \n            \n              Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/explore-gel-plate-printing
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
