DESCRIPTION:FREE - No ticket required Parking permit required\, visit the 
 SSU parking permit webpage. Join us for our annual Family Day festival\, a
  free\, bilingual celebration that includes fun and engaging performances\
 , interactive activities\, and workshops. This event will feature a vibran
 t\, educational performance by SF-based dance and music ensemble La Mezcla
 \, which brings together tap dance\, son jarocho \\(music and dance tradit
 ion from Veracruz\, MX\\)\, and Afro-Caribbean rhythms and movement. There
  will also be a performance and workshops led by Play Marimba!\, dance dem
 onstrations by Grupo Folklorico Quetzalen\, and a variety of activities le
 d by Sonoma State education students\, SSU's Center for Environmental Inqu
 iry\, Raizes Collective\, PBS Kids\, and the Sonoma County Library for chi
 ldren of all ages
