BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/rent-school-edition-musical/18179688/2026-03-28T19", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/rent-school-edition-musical/18179688/2026-03-28T19"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/rent-school-edition-musical/18179688/2026-03-28T19"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:"Rent School Edition"- Musical
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T190000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T220000
UID:260305kzGEBG1-7063Hf4GwA8ZJg
DESCRIPTION:Set in the East Village of New York City\, Rent School Edition
  is about falling in love\, finding your voice and living for today. Winne
 r of the Tony Award for Best Musical and the Pulitzer Prize for Drama\, it
  has become a pop cultural phenomenon with songs that rock and a story tha
 t resonates with audiences of all ages.\n\nBased loosely on Puccini’s La
  Boheme\, Rent School Edition follows a year in the life of a group of imp
 overished young artists and musicians struggling to survive and create in 
 New York’s Lower East Side\, under the shadow of HIV/AIDS. The physical 
 and emotional complications of the disease pervade the lives of Roger\, Mi
 mi\, Tom and Angel. Maureen deals with her chronic infidelity through perf
 ormance art\; her partner\, Joanne\, wonders if their relationship is wort
 h the trouble. Benny has sold out his Bohemian ideals in exchange for a he
 fty income and is on the outs with his former friends. Mark\, an aspiring 
 filmmaker\, feels like an outsider to life in general. How these young boh
 emians negotiate their dreams\, loves and conflicts provides the narrative
  thread to this groundbreaking musical.\n\nCredits\n\nBook\, Music\, and L
 yrics by Jonathan Larson\n\nDirected by Kele Gasparini\n\nEnjoy our LIVE P
 it Orchestra\n\nTickets: GoFan.CO \n\nhttps://gofan.co/app/school/CA23048
 \n\nSuggested Audience Age 13\\+\n\nContent Warnings\n\nAdult Themes\, Dri
 nking\, Drugs & Smoking\, Mild Language
LOCATION:San Marin High - Emily Gates Performing Arts Center
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/rent-school-edition-mus
 ical/18179688/2026-03-28T19
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://shop.coyotesonoma.com/country-line-dancing-with-dustin-saylor--the-stowaways-328-p216.aspx", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/country-line-dancing-night-ft-dustin-saylor-the-stowaways/18242193/2026-03-28T19"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://shop.coyotesonoma.com/country-line-dancing-with-dustin-saylor--the-stowaways-328-p216.aspx"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Country Line Dancing Night ft. Dustin Saylor & The Stowaways
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T190000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T190000
UID:260228LvBHmzcMxkSUTQW7Zw_PNA
DESCRIPTION:**Date:** Saturday\, March 28\, 2026\n\n**Time:** Doors 6 PM 
 | Lessons 7-8 PM | Live music throughout the night\n\n**Tickets:** $20 Adv
 ance | $25 Door | Coyote Sonoma Members Receive $5 Off\n\nJoin us for line
  dancing lessons from Grapevine Dance! Plus live music from Dustin Saylor 
 & The Stowaways.\n\nAbout Dustin Saylor:\n\nDustin Saylor\, a Northern Cal
 ifornia-born country singer-songwriter\, has made a name for himself as th
 e #1 Country/Folk artist in the San Francisco Bay Area. His musical journe
 y began in childhood\, first at the piano and later as a guitarist and sin
 ger for his high school youth group and local church. Despite early challe
 nges\, including a devastating American Idol rejection in 2009\, Saylor ha
 d a transformative moment on his long drive home\, realizing that true suc
 cess required full commitment. Embracing his calling\, he quit bartending\
 , pursued a music degree at Sonoma State University\, and became a full-ti
 me musician. Over the years\, he has performed alongside artists like Tyle
 r Rich\, Chase Rice\, and Daughtry\, with his sound often compared to Thom
 as Rhett and Chris Stapleton. His songwriting is deeply personal\, shaped 
 by his early experiences of adoption and the contrasting struggles and joy
 s of his life. Through his music\, Saylor seeks to inspire\, heal\, and cr
 eate a space where people can connect beyond labels. Committed to his craf
 t\, he remains "all in\," determined to sing and play music for the rest o
 f his life.
LOCATION:Coyote Sonoma
URL:https://shop.coyotesonoma.com/country-line-dancing-with-dustin-saylor-
 -the-stowaways-328-p216.aspx
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/t-bone-n-weasel-live-theatre/18156402/2026-03-28T19", "Press Democrat": "https://the222.org/product/t-bone-n-weasel/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/t-bone-n-weasel-live-theatre/18156402/2026-03-28T19"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:T-Bone N Weasel - Live Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T190000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T190000
UID:260219BKJP2U5Ch0eBr6D5e6yOGA
DESCRIPTION:The play follows the antic peregrinations of two ex-convicts a
 s they make their erratic way across South Carolina in search of a hot mea
 l or an easy mark.\n\nHoping to bring themselves up to at least the povert
 y level\, two ex-convicts\, T Bone \\(who is Black\\) and Weasel \\(who is
  White\\) have stolen a rather decrepit Buick and have set off across Sout
 h Carolina with minor mayhem in mind. Moving swiftly from one adventure t
 o another\, they botch an attempted robbery\,  are swindled out of the Bu
 ick by a fast-talking used car dealer\, run afoul of a sexually voracious 
 lady farmer\, fall into the clutches of a larcenous country preacher\, and
  try to make off with the automobile of a politically ambitious small town
  doctor who wants to exhibit them as examples of what poverty can do to pe
 ople. Then it is back on the road again…\n\nEvery time they try to break
  the law\, the law breaks them. A tale of two idiots\, smartly told by pla
 ywright Jon Klein\, “T-Bone n Weasel” is kind of like a good road-kill
 : it’s funny\, gross and makes a lasting impression. — Variety\n\nFeat
 uring:\n\nT-Bone – Aldo Billingslea\n\nWeasel – Timothy Redman\n\nVern
 a Mae – Sylvia Burboeck\n\nSponsored by Linda Hillel & Jon Eisenberg and
  Malin Giddings & Richard Hechler\n\nTheatre - Programmed by Aldo Billings
 lea and Amy Kossow\n\nTHE 222 / 222 Healdsburg Avenue / Healdsburg CA
LOCATION:THE 222 / Healdsburg
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/t-bone-n-weasel-live-th
 eatre/18156402/2026-03-28T19
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
