BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Uptowntheatrenapa": "https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/jam-cellars-presents-cristela-alonzo-the-midlife-mixtape-tour/", "North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/cristela-alonzo-the-midlife-mixtape-tour/17499706/2026-03-28T19"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Uptowntheatrenapa": "https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/jam-cellars-presents-cristela-alonzo-the-midlife-mixtape-tour/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:uptowntheatrenapa
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Uptowntheatrenapa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260328T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260328T193000
DTSTAMP:20260317T222428
CREATED:20251117T180005Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251118T043509Z
UID:25389-1774726200-1774726200@www.uptowntheatrenapa.com
SUMMARY:Cristela Alonzo: The Midlife Mixtape Tour
DESCRIPTION:March 28\, 2026\nPURCHASE TICKETS HERE  \nDoors 6:30pm/ Show 7:30pm\nAges: 12+ \nCristela Alonzo is a powerhouse comedian\, writer\, and actress whose sharp wit and infectious charm have made her a standout voice in comedy today. Most recently\, she served as a co-producer on Happy’ s Place and continues to bring her unique perspective to screens big and small. \nHer latest Netflix comedy special\, Upper Classy\, premiered on September 23\, following the success of her previous hits Middle Classy and Lower Classy — a trilogy that hilariously traces her journey from humble beginnings to unapologetic self-awareness. \nOn the acting front\, Cristela has appeared in Netflix’s The Laundromat\, starring alongside legends Meryl Streep and Gary Oldman\, and before that\, she made history as the creator and star of her own ABC sitcom\, Cristela. \nA regular favorite on The View and a familiar face from Conan\, Cristela has also been featured on Comedy Central’s Live at Gotham\, Gabriel Iglesias Presents Stand-Up Revolution\, and Showtime’s Legally Brown. Her work behind the camera has earned her multiple awards\, including Best Film at the Boston Comedy Festival for her short films. \nCristela’s range even extends into drama; she appeared in FX’s acclaimed series Sons of Anarchy\, but her heart always brings her back to the stage. She’s currently touring the country with her latest stand-up tour\, The Midlife Mixtape Tour\, proving that comedy\, like life\, only gets better with experience.
URL:https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/jam-cellars-presents-cristela-alonzo-the-midlife-mixtape-tour/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/CA_1200x800.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://theimaginists.org/the-naturalists-march-april", "Press Democrat": "https://theimaginists.org/the-naturalists-march-april"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://theimaginists.org/the-naturalists-march-april"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Imaginists present The Naturalists a new play by Jon Bernson
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T220000
UID:260309C2gmMYn44UOf-aLXXHs7HA
DESCRIPTION:The Imaginists present a new play by Jon Bernson about a reclu
 sive group of scientists whose radical discoveries challenge widely held a
 ssumptions about the world.The play unfolds across two interwoven timeline
 s: in the present\, the audience witnesses a sequence of high-stakes lectu
 res\, as each scientist unveils work that promises to reshape reality itse
 lf. Between these presentations\, the story flashes back to the week befor
 e the summit\, marked by the recent death of one of the Naturalists and es
 calating financial strain that threatens their fragile order.
LOCATION:The Imaginists
URL:https://theimaginists.org/the-naturalists-march-april
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-menagerie/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Glass Menagerie
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T213000
UID:2602276wQTocZVhkmmHQKXVlBK7A
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 Season at Curtain Call Theatre starts off with **The 
 Glass Menagerie**\, the play that made Tennessee Williams famous.\n\nHave 
 You Ever Felt Stuck Between Your Dreams and Reality? This Play Gets It.\n\
 nImagine being trapped in a tiny apartment during the Great Depression —
  no money\, no way out\, just a family clinging to hopes that may never co
 me true. That's exactly what The Glass Menagerie is about.\n\nWritten by T
 ennessee Williams — one of America's greatest playwrights — this story
  follows a restless son\, an overbearing mom\, and a painfully shy daughte
 r as they each chase dreams that feel just out of reach. It's emotional\, 
 poetic\, and honestly… kind of hits different when you think about your 
 own life.\n\nThis iconic play is literally studied in classrooms worldwide
 \, so seeing it live is like watching your textbook come to life — excep
 t way more powerful.\n\n📅 March 13–29\, 2026\n\n📍 20347 Hwy 116\, 
 Monte Rio\, CA\n\n🎟️ Grab your tickets at russianriverhall.com or cal
 l (707) 387-5072\n\nThe Glass Menagerie by Tennessee Williams is directed 
 by Michael Tabib.\n\nShowing at the Russian River Hall in Monte Rio\, CA f
 rom March 13-29\, 2026.\n\nProgram was made possible\, in part\, with fund
 s from Creative Sonoma and the California Arts Council (CAC).\n\nBy specia
 l arrangement with Dramatists Play Services\, Inc.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/2026/02/18/march-13-29-the-glass-mena
 gerie/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://www.cloverdaleperformingarts.com/events/comedy-night-joe-klocek"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Comedy Night at Cloverdale Performing Arts Center - Featuring Joe 
 Klocek
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T193000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260328T213000
UID:260308MMWqI7-iPUiuX4EovjjfoQ
DESCRIPTION:Joe is a square peg in a round hole sort of guy. Raised a Midw
 esterner\, so he has manners\, but living in San Francisco for more than 3
 0 years\, so he thinks he's better than you. Joe does two things great —
  tells stories and talks to the crowd.\n\nJoe currently runs two monthly s
 hows in San Francisco. At Cobbs Comedy Club\, his game show\, “Get It!?
 ” is becoming the next big thing. At The Punch Line\, Joe Klocek & Frien
 ds\, is his chance to show off new talent to audiences and headline.\n\nJo
 e had a two month "comic in residency" at the first comedy club in Shangha
 i\, China.\n\nJoe has been featured on NPR's\, "Snap Judgement" and has al
 so appeared on Comedy Central's "Live at Gotham\," NBC's "Last Comic Stand
 ing\," and was commentator for the Emmy award winning documentary\, "A Bri
 dge So Far."\n\nJoe has also been a runner-up in the "San Francisco Intern
 ational Comedy Competition" and the "Seattle Comedy Competition." \n\nVot
 ed "Best Comic" in the SF Weekly Readers Poll.
LOCATION:Cloverdale Performing Arts Center
URL:https://www.cloverdaleperformingarts.com/events/comedy-night-joe-kloce
 k
