BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://hwhorses-middle-school.eventbrite.com", "Press Democrat": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/hanging-with-horses-middle-school-tickets-1982833131272?aff=oddtdtcreator"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://hwhorses-middle-school.eventbrite.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Hanging with Horses: Middle School
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T103000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T120000
UID:260305Uzm7-_BUcE67mkHBtsRC0Q
DESCRIPTION:Middle school can be… a lot. Friendships changing. Siblings.
  Academic stress. Anxious moments. Parents. You know. Horses are amazing f
 riends\, guides\, listeners\, and healers. They really know about relation
 ships. AND they are experts at stress management. Hanging with Horses: Mid
 dle School is a three-week group meeting consecutively on Sundays\, March 
 15-29\, 10:30 AM\, on a beautiful old cattle ranch between Novato and Peta
 luma. If you join **Hanging with Horses**\, you will have a blast and beco
 me a part of a wonderful herd (horses and humans.) You might also...\n\nTr
 y grounding and relaxation tools that actually help.\n\nBuild confidence a
 nd leadership—just by being yourself.\n\nLearn to speak horse while cari
 ng for the herd.\n\nYou don’t have to talk if you’re not ready. You do
 n’t have to be “good with people.” You don’t need any horse experi
 ence.\n\nJust come as you are. The horses will meet you there 🐎✨\n\nT
 hrough unpressured time “hanging with horses\,” guided group conversat
 ions\, and hands-on experiences\, participants will learn to:\n\nUnderstan
 d what stress and anxiety feel like in their own bodies\n\nBuild healthier
  friendships and boundaries\n\nDevelop emotional awareness and leadership 
 skills\n\nPractice grounding and calming tools they can use anywhere\n\nGa
 in confidence by tuning into themselves and their environment\n\nHorses na
 turally reflect emotions and stress levels\, giving kids a powerful (and n
 on-judgmental) way to learn about themselves and others.\n\n🐎**NEIGH**:
  You can schedule a call to speak with the director of Heart & Mind Equine
  to learn more and see if this group is a good option for your family. Sch
 edule here.\n\nScholarships are available. Please reach out or schedule a 
 call to request- HeartMindEquine@gmail.com\n\nLearn more and register here
 : https://hwhorses-middle-school.eventbrite.com
LOCATION:Heart & Mind Equine Horse Rescue
URL:https://hwhorses-middle-school.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://ushergallerypetaluma.com/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Local Author Read Aloud: Bubbles with Andre Morrow
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T110000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T120000
UID:260316MmW-gPuySkudNDMTG8gKZw
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Sunday\, March 29th\, from 11am-12pm\, for a fun ch
 ildren’s read-aloud of Bubbles by local author André Morrow! All are we
 lcome to join us in reading and celebrating this musical tale. We’ll be 
 featuring live children’s songs\, snacks\, and an engaging storytime.  
 “Bubbles” is a whimsical story that teaches young readers to appreciat
 e all the wonderful little things in life\, like playing with pets and fam
 ily\, blowing bubbles\, and enjoying the outdoors. The story highlights gr
 atitude in a playful and educational way!\n\nRead more about the precious 
 story of how Bubbles came to be\, quoted directly from the author:\n\n " 
 Bubbles is a song\, video and children's book. The "Bubbles" project began
  during a visit with some of my grandkids\, Hadley Dickson\, James Dickson
 \, and Danica Dickson. Most of our visits include music time and taking a 
 whack at writing songs together. On this particular visit\, we'd just fini
 shed an enthusiastic adventure making bubbles in the backyard. Afterward\,
  during music time\, I asked them what they wanted to write about and one 
 of them yelled out "Bubbles". And the song was born. Months later\, my mus
 ic partner David J. Michalak and I began producing the song to add to our 
 collection of music. My cousins\, Sophia Bass and Catherine Bass\, sisters
 \, both wonderful artists\, agreed to assist us with the project. Catherin
 e is an amazing painter and Sophia's voice is incomparable. They are the d
 aughters of my cousin Reggie Bass who was my great friend and music partne
 r of my youth. So together we all created the Bubbles book\, song\, and vi
 deo. We hope you enjoy it! The song can be found on all major music platfo
 rms using the artist's name Morrow Michalak. The video can be found at mor
 rowmichalak.com/bubbles. Thanks to Barb Schacht\, who heard an early rendi
 tion of the song and suggested it would make a terrific kid's book. ”\n\
 nWishing you Butterflies\, Sunshine\, and Rainbows\, André \\(Papi\\) Mor
 row
LOCATION:Usher Gallery
URL:https://ushergallerypetaluma.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://personalspace.space/exhibitions/glyph"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:GLYPH  - Art Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T110000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T150000
UID:2603105dDpdJonTkujN9evBPWxew
DESCRIPTION:Glyph will be on view through May 3. Personal Space is open Su
 ndays 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. and by appointment.\n\nBig news! Personal Space is
  back from our \\(much needed\\) hiatus. Join us next Sunday\, March 15 \
 \(2-5pm\\) for the opening of  Glyph. This is our first opening since Vil
 lage opened up next door\, and it’s sure to be a party!\n\nFeaturing thi
 rteen artists from the Bay Area and beyond\, Glyph embraces a liminal spac
 e which allows subconscious connections to reign and centers gut feeling a
 s a source of poetry\, mystery\, and magic. Collectively\, these artists d
 raw from an enigmatic lexicon of symbols\, favoring inscrutable familiarit
 y over anything known or quantified. This intuitive language manifests thr
 ough a varied approach to material translation that underscores\, and cele
 brates\, our innate ability to understand things deeply without having to 
 define them in words.\n\nGlyph features works by:\n\nSadie Buckner \n\nLu
 is Estrada \n\nRochele Gomez \n\nKainoa Gruspe \n\nLéonie Guyer \n\nK
 lea McKenna\n\nMitzi Pederson \n\nBen Peterson \n\nJ Pendleton\n\nRobert
  Smithson \n\nEmma Spertus \n\nHenna Vainio \n\nRichard Zimmerman \n\n
 See link for details and artist bios.
LOCATION:Personal Space
URL:https://personalspace.space/exhibitions/glyph
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
