X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/t-bone-n-weasel-live-theatre/18156402/2026-03-29T14", "Press Democrat": "https://the222.org/product/t-bone-n-weasel/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/t-bone-n-weasel-live-theatre/18156402/2026-03-29T14"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:T-Bone N Weasel - Live Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T140000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T140000
UID:260219hp03Cnjk40StmK7PpIn2aA
DESCRIPTION:The play follows the antic peregrinations of two ex-convicts a
 s they make their erratic way across South Carolina in search of a hot mea
 l or an easy mark.\n\nHoping to bring themselves up to at least the povert
 y level\, two ex-convicts\, T Bone \\(who is Black\\) and Weasel \\(who is
  White\\) have stolen a rather decrepit Buick and have set off across Sout
 h Carolina with minor mayhem in mind. Moving swiftly from one adventure t
 o another\, they botch an attempted robbery\,  are swindled out of the Bu
 ick by a fast-talking used car dealer\, run afoul of a sexually voracious 
 lady farmer\, fall into the clutches of a larcenous country preacher\, and
  try to make off with the automobile of a politically ambitious small town
  doctor who wants to exhibit them as examples of what poverty can do to pe
 ople. Then it is back on the road again…\n\nEvery time they try to break
  the law\, the law breaks them. A tale of two idiots\, smartly told by pla
 ywright Jon Klein\, “T-Bone n Weasel” is kind of like a good road-kill
 : it’s funny\, gross and makes a lasting impression. — Variety\n\nFeat
 uring:\n\nT-Bone – Aldo Billingslea\n\nWeasel – Timothy Redman\n\nVern
 a Mae – Sylvia Burboeck\n\nSponsored by Linda Hillel & Jon Eisenberg and
  Malin Giddings & Richard Hechler\n\nTheatre - Programmed by Aldo Billings
 lea and Amy Kossow\n\nTHE 222 / 222 Healdsburg Avenue / Healdsburg CA
LOCATION:THE 222 / Healdsburg
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/t-bone-n-weasel-live-th
 eatre/18156402/2026-03-29T14
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/marjorie-prime/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Marjorie Prime
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T140000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T152000
UID:250801j4feTGpTUU-ZRmgbsfYP3Q
DESCRIPTION:**Artificial Remembrance: The Intersection of Technology and M
 emory**\n\n***“Jordan Harrison’s gently uncanny play imagines a future
  solution for a person in mourning: the recreation of someone you love as 
 an artificial intelligence.”* —Kate Wyver\, The Guardian**\n\n**In *Ma
 rjorie Prime*\, playwright Jordan Harrison delves into the intricate dance
  between human memory and artificial intelligence. Set in the not-so-dista
 nt future\, the narrative centers on 85-year-old Marjorie\, whose mind is 
 gradually succumbing to dementia. To combat her fading recollections\, her
  family introduces her to a “Prime”—a lifelike holographic projectio
 n of her late husband\, Walter\, programmed to retell the stories of their
  shared past. As Marjorie interacts with Walter Prime\, the lines between 
 authentic memories and reconstructed narratives blur\, prompting profound 
 questions about identity\, the reliability of our recollections\, and the 
 extent to which technology can replicate the essence of human connection. 
 This thought-provoking drama challenges audiences to consider what we choo
 se to remember\, what we wish to forget\, and how the digital age reshapes
  the very fabric of our personal histories.**\n\n***Marjorie Prime* has ga
 rnered critical acclaim for its insightful exploration and profound commen
 tary on the human condition in an era where technology increasingly intert
 wines with our daily lives.**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays & Saturdays @ 7:30pm\
 , Saturdays and Sundays at 2:00pm Run Time: One hour\, 20 mins including i
 ntermission\n\nThursdays Adult $33 Fri/Sat Eve Adult $39.95\; Senior $36.9
 5\; Under 18 $26.95 Sat/Sun Matinee Adult $47.95\; Senior $44.95 \\*All pr
 ices include fees (707) 523-4185 **boxoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/marjorie-prime/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
