BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Uptowntheatrenapa": "https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/patton-oswalt-effervescent/", "North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/patton-oswalt-effervescent/17654649/2026-04-01T20"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Uptowntheatrenapa": "https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/patton-oswalt-effervescent/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:uptowntheatrenapa
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Uptowntheatrenapa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260401T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260401T200000
DTSTAMP:20260317T222428
CREATED:20251209T180402Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251209T193705Z
UID:25456-1775073600-1775073600@www.uptowntheatrenapa.com
SUMMARY:Patton Oswalt: Effervescent
DESCRIPTION:April 1\, 2026\nPURCHASE TICKETS HERE  \nDoors 7pm/ Show 8pm\nAges: 12+ \nPatton Oswalt continues to leave his distinctive imprint across all areas of entertainment\, from his award-winning comedy specials to his many guest roles on television. His most recent comedy special We All Scream (which also marked his directorial debut) launched on Netflix last September and Oswalt was recently nominated for a Grammy for his comedy album. Last year\, he starred in the Magnolia Pictures comedy I Love My Dad\, winner of the Grand Jury and Audience awards at the 2022 SXSW Film Festival. \nOswalt was nominated for a Critics Choice Award for his performance in Jason Reitman’s film Young Adult\, starring opposite Charlize Theron. In 2009\, he also received critical acclaim for his performance in Robert Siegel’s Big Fan; the film was nominated for an Independent Spirit Award and Oswalt earned a Gotham Award nomination for his performance. \nOswalt has appeared in many films\, including The Circle\, alongside Tom Hanks\, The Secret Life of Walter Mitty and Zoolander\, both directed by Ben Stiller\, Steven Soderbergh’s The Informant with Matt Damon\, and alongside Seth Rogen in Jody Hill’s Observe and Report\, as well as Paul Thomas Anderson’s Magnolia and Todd Phillips’ Starsky and Hutch. \nOswalt’s past television work includes memorable roles on Parks and Recreation\, which brought him a TV Critics Choice Award\, A.P. Bio\, Veep\, United States of Tara\, Seinfeld (his TV acting debut)\, and many more. He is also very well known for playing ‘Spence’ on The King of Queens for nine seasons. Oswalt is also the narrator on ABC’s hit comedy The Goldbergs. He provided the voice for ‘Remy’ the rat in Pixar’s Oscar® winner Ratatouille\, and his other voice credits include ‘Max’ in The Secret Life of Pets 2\, Sorry To Bother You\, the SYFY series Happy!\, Rick and Morty\, Archer\, and BoJack Horseman. \nIn 2020\, Oswalt’s Emmy-nominated Netflix special I Love Everything was widely applauded upon release\, and he received a Grammy nomination for his comedy album of the same name. In 2017\, he received Grammy and Emmy nominations for his album and Netflix special Annihilation\, which addresses his own devastating loss and dealing with the unexplainable\, while making it all painfully funny. In 2016\, he won the Emmy for ‘Outstanding Writing for a Variety Special’ for his sixth comedy special Talking for Clapping and a Grammy Award in 2017 for his comedy album. He has been nominated for a total of six Grammys and four Emmys. Oswalt has shot eight TV specials and released seven critically acclaimed albums — in 2009\, Patton received his first Grammy nomination for his album My Weakness Is Strong.
URL:https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/patton-oswalt-effervescent/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/PO_1200x800-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.stcolumbasinverness.org/triduum"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Triduum and Easter Celebrations
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260401T200000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260401T210000
UID:260218EgXvSYzmgkmQ2r0CHxiZXw
DESCRIPTION:As we approach the highest holy days of the Christian year\, w
 e warmly invite you to join St. Columba’s\, Inverness for the celebratio
 n of the Sacred Triduum\, culminating in the joy of Easter Sunday. The Tri
 duum \\(Latin for “three days”\\) is one continuous liturgy unfolding 
 over Maundy Thursday\, Good Friday\, and the Great Vigil of Easter. Togeth
 er\, these services celebrate the history of salvation from Creation to Re
 demption. A history of Love poured out\, suffering faced with courage\, de
 ath held in hope\, and new life in the most unexpected of places. \n\nAll
  services are open to the public.\n\nMaundy Thursday – April 1 | 8:00 pm
 \n\nLiturgy & Washing of the Feet\n\nWe gather to remember Jesus’ final 
 meal with his friends and his commandment to love through humble service. 
 The washing of feet invites us into vulnerability\, care\, and shared huma
 nity.\n\nGood Friday – April 2 | 12:00 pm & 3:00 pm\n\n12:00 pm – Outd
 oor Ecological Way of the Cross\n\nWe walk together outdoors\, praying wit
 h creation and reflecting on suffering\, grief\, and our shared responsibi
 lity for the healing of the earth.\n\n3:00 pm – Veneration of the Cross 
 \\(in the nave\\)\n\nA solemn and spacious liturgy where we honor the myst
 ery of the cross and the depth of Christ’s love.\n\nHoly Saturday – Ap
 ril 3 | 8:00 pm\n\nThe Great Vigil of Easter & Celebratory Reception\n\nBe
 ginning in darkness\, we tell the great stories of salvation\, light the n
 ew fire\, renew baptismal promises\, and proclaim the Resurrection. A cele
 bratory reception follows as we rejoice together.\n\nEaster Sunday – Apr
 il 4 | 10:00 am\n\nLiturgy of the Resurrection & Easter Brunch\n\nWe celeb
 rate the triumph of life over death\, hope over despair\, and love over fe
 ar. Easter Brunch follows. Come and feast with us.\n\nIf you are longing f
 or meaning\, beauty\, or hope in these dark days\, you belong here. Come a
 s you are. Bring a friend. Walk with us from the table to the cross and th
 e empty tomb.
LOCATION:St. Columba's Inverness
URL:https://www.stcolumbasinverness.org/triduum
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
