BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/pt-1-modifying-thrown-forms-focusing-on-teapot-making-with-ping-zhong"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Pt 1: Modifying Thrown Forms – Focusing on Teapot Making with Pi
 ng Zhong — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260404T000000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260405T000000
UID:81a08918255eb485ea08eceb0201e603@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Pt 1: Modifying Thrown Forms – Focusing on Teapot Making wit
 h Ping Zhong\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $10.00\n        \n  
     \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, April 4\, 2026\; 10am-11amLocated in the Cera
 mics StudioIn this workshop\, SebArts’ Ceramics Residency artist\, Ping 
 Zhong\, will focus on the details and assembly of a teapot. Due to time an
 d space considerations\, wheel-throwing will not be demonstrated on site. 
 Instead\, pre-thrown pot bodies will be prepared as starting points. The w
 orkshop will center on shaping small components such as knobs\, spouts\, a
 nd handles\, including hand-building techniques for forming these parts\, 
 as well as methods for attaching them harmoniously to the body. The instru
 ctor will also share practical tool tips to help participants work confide
 ntly with fine details and achieve a polished finish. This workshop is rec
 ommended to be held shortly after the instructor’s arrival.Due to limite
 d capacity of the Ceramics Studio\, we are asking for a suggested donation
  of $10 to confirm your attendance. About the Artist: Ping Zhong’s artis
 tic practice is a continuous exploration of regeneration—of materials\, 
 forms\, and cultural narratives. She investigates the dialogue between anc
 ient Chinese pottery and contemporary visual language\, using wheel-throwi
 ng\, hand-building\, and sculpture to create works in which history and pe
 rsonal growth converge. This reinterpretation of classical forms is not on
 ly an artistic method\, but also a philosophical inquiry into the harmony 
 between past and future. Deeply motivated to uncover the potential within 
 clay\, Ping pushes the boundaries of design and technique. Her work reflec
 ts on universal themes: the individual’s place within the community\, th
 e relationship between essence and appearance\, and the evolving connectio
 n between nature and society. Through these explorations\, she seeks to cr
 eate art that resonates across cultures.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        \n          \n            \n      
         Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/pt-1-modifying-thrown-forms-f
 ocusing-on-teapot-making-with-ping-zhong
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/collage-on-panel-from-start-to-finish-44"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Collage on Panel from Start to Finish — Sebastopol Center For th
 e Arts\, California
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260404T000000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260405T000000
UID:981db32cbd17d4b42a797130c9cbe458@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Collage on Panel from Start to Finish\, 4/4\n\n  \n    \n     
  \n        \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, A
 pril 4\, 2026\; 11 AM - 3 PMFee: $115 + $15 materials feeAge: 16+ \, Locat
 ion: P/D RoomJoin French-American collage artist Catherine Cruz for a new 
 comprehensive collage workshop designed to to guide you through the comple
 te process of creating a finished collage on wood panel. Her hands-on proc
 ess will cover every step—from surface preparation and design to varnish
 ing and wiring.  You will learn presentation tips to give your artwork a p
 rofessional finish.  What you’ll obtain from this workshop: Reliable met
 hods for preparing your panel\, Technical information about selected art m
 aterials\, Creative ways to explore abstraction through collage\, Techniqu
 es for presenting your art.IMPORTANT: Each participant must purchase and b
 ring the following items listed in the attached PDF.  The class will begin
  with a demonstration\, so please plan to arrive early to allow time to se
 ttle in.A short lunch break will be held from 12:30 to 1:00 PM. Kindly bri
 ng your own lunch and beverage.About the instructor: Catherine Cruz is a F
 rench-American artist whose work is informed by textures and patterns crea
 ted by the passing of time and the effects of the natural elements on the 
 built environment.  She holds a Bachelor of Science in interior design and
  she worked in the field of architectural design and green building certif
 ication for over 25 years.  She has taught collage and mixed media worksho
 ps in the Bay Area and in France since 2019\, and this is her fifth year a
 t the Sebastopol Center for the Arts.  Her studio is located in Sebastopol
  and she participates in Art Trails Open Studios.  You may contact Catheri
 ne at beyouartstudio@gmail.com.  Check out Catherine’s other classes her
 e:  https://wwws.sebarts.org/visual-arts-classes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        \n          \n           
  \n              Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/collage-on-panel-from-start-t
 o-finish-44
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
