SUMMARY: Beginning Gel Printing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Magdalena Bogart\nMonday\, April 6th\n1:00pm-4:00
 PM\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n$45.00\n\n\nJoin us for an inspiring gel 
 printing workshop with Magdalena Bogart\, where you'll discover the\nmagi
 c of this versatile and expressive art form. You will learn techniques fo
 r creating stunning\,\nlayered prints using gel plates\, rich textures\, 
 and vibrant colors.\nIf you have wanted to try out this fairly new and ve
 ry popular way to make your own papers\, whether you are an experienced a
 rtist or simply curious about the process\, this workshop will provide pl
 enty of creative inspiration and expert insights.\n\nDuring the 3-hours w
 orkshop\, you will learn the fundamentals of mono-printing with a gel pla
 te\,\nincluding an in-depth look at the essential supplies needed. Magdal
 ena will discuss different\ntypes of plates and brayers\, as well as the 
 wide range of acrylic paints and inks. You will learn the basics of color
  theory to ensure great results for your projects.\n\nYou will get to try
  out many fun techniques on different papers. Magdalena will introduce va
 rious papers for gel printing\, including white copy paper\, calligraphy 
 paper\, deli paper\, marker paper\, and more each offering unique effects
 .\n\nThe workshop will also explore tools for making marks and textures\,
  from found objects to store-bought supplies. Magdalena will demonstrate 
 how to use stencils - both handmade and purchased\, along with unconventi
 onal tools like silicone scrapers\, scrapers\, bubble wrap\, buttons\, ya
 rn\, and cardboard to create stunning patterns.\n\nShe will also cover te
 chniques to embellish your prints incorporating acrylic pens\, Inktense p
 encils and other techniques.\nAdditionally\, Magdalena will provide exper
 t guidance on cleaning\, caring for\, and storing gel plates to ensure th
 eir longevity. To wrap up the session\, she will showcase creative ways t
 o use your printed papers\, including ideas for collages\, handmade cards
 \, and art journals\, along with a take-home list of even more ways to in
 corporate your gel prints into future projects. Whether you are looking t
 o refine your skills or try something new\, this workshop promises to be 
 an engaging and educational experience. Come explore the endless possibil
 ities of gel printing.\n\n\nTo register for this workshop\, please contac
 t Magdalena at: 408.781.2589 or by email\nat: mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com
  mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com mailto:mag.bogar
 t@gmail.com mag.bogart@gmail.com mailto:mag.bogart@gmail.com mailto:mag.b
 ogart@gmail.com
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,gel-printing
