X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/600035/citrus-curd-workshop-with-merrilee-olson", "Press Democrat": "https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/600035/citrus-curd-workshop-with-merrilee-olson"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/600035/citrus-curd-workshop-with-merrilee-olson"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Making Citrus Curd with Merrilee Olson at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260410T100000
DTEND;TZID=PDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260410T130000
UID:260313Sx_5Kkc7kkS39zPzUGMSBA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a hands-on citrus curd making class led by chef an
 d food preservationist Merrilee Olson. Over three hours\, Merrilee will gu
 ide you through every step of making silky\, vibrant citrus curd — shari
 ng her expert techniques and secrets for achieving that perfect balance of
  tart\, sweet\, and luscious — using organic Meyer Lemons grown right he
 re on our 88-acre farm.\n\nThe experience begins with a ride aboard our ap
 ple-themed trolley out to the Apple Cottage\, where the class takes place 
 surrounded by the beauty of the farm. Each guest will take home an apple-b
 lossom pink apron\, a jar of the curd they made\, and a bag of fresh organ
 ic lemons to put your new skills to the test!\n\nMerrilee Olson is a chef 
 and food preservationist with years of experience transforming farm-fresh 
 ingredients into culinary treasures. As the founder of Preserve Farm Kitch
 ens\, she has dedicated her work to celebrating seasonal produce and the t
 imeless art of preservation\, bringing creativity\, expertise\, and a deep
  love of good food to every class she teaches.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/600035/citr
 us-curd-workshop-with-merrilee-olson
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
