SUMMARY:Migrations: Birds and Words on Oona-pa’is (Sonoma Mountain)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260412T110000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260412T110000
UID:2a8d2a0ecea7c2e19a3f1d0cd5e3886c@jacklondonpark.com
DESCRIPTION:“Migratory birds connect people\, ecosystems\, and nations. 
 They are symbols of peace and an interconnected planet.” —Antonio Gute
 rres Migrations have been integral to wild and human lives on Oona-pa’i
 s for millennia. Following favorable climate\, familial ties\, and food av
 ailability is necessary to a community’s survival and healthy diversity.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park\, 2400 London Ranch Road\, Glen E
 llen\, CA 95442
