BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Uptowntheatrenapa": "https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/jam-cellars-presents-sierra-hull/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:uptowntheatrenapa
X-SOURCE:Uptowntheatrenapa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T200000
DTSTAMP:20260317T222428
CREATED:20251209T170147Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260210T061301Z
UID:25462-1776542400-1776542400@www.uptowntheatrenapa.com
SUMMARY:JaM Cellars Presents Sierra Hull with support from Mason Via
DESCRIPTION:APRIL 18\, 2026\nPURCHASE TICKETS HERE  \nDoors 7pm/ Show 8pm\nAges: 12+ \nSierra Hull is a seven-time IBMA Mandolin Player of the Year and six-time Grammy nominee\, one of bluegrass and Americana’s most dynamic voices. Her latest album\, A Tip Toe High Wire\, her first independent release\, highlights her songwriting and instrumental mastery\, featuring Béla Fleck\, Tim O’Brien\, and Aoife O’Donovan. The album is nominated for four GRAMMY Awards\, balancing tradition with innovation. \nHull has shared stages with Alison Krauss\, Eric Clapton\, Sturgill Simpson\, Slash\, and Robert Randolph\, and performed on NPR’s Tiny Desk and The Kelly Clarkson Show. She is the first female artist with a Gibson signature mandolin and a Tennessee Governor’s Distinguished Arts Award recipient. \nWith support from Mason Via \nMason Via’s new single\, “Wide Open.” Co-written by Mason Via and Zach John King \, this track paints vivid pictures of campfires\, screen doors\, and sunsets over pastures\, while also capturing the essence of young heartbreak. Raised in Patrick Springs\, VA\, Mason drew on his childhood experiences growing up in the hills\, hollers\, and backwoods of southern Virginia to inspire this incredible new song. Via says\, “The song chronicles the singer’s emotional state as he reaches back into his memory to recall how much he loved the girl who has left him\, and how much her absence has cut him to the core.” This song evokes a similiar emotion that Mason conveyed in Daughter of the Highlands (his stand out vocal on the Grammy nominated album Jubilee.) The track features Mason Via on lead vocals and guitar; Aaron Ramsey on mandolin; Jason Davis on banjo; Jim Vancleve on fiddle; Jeff Partin on bass and resophonic guitar; Kyser George on second guitar; Brooks Forsyth on harmony vocals; and Nick Goad on harmony vocals. This track sounds like Old Crow Medicine Show\, Tyler Childers \, Zach Bryan\, Flatland Cavalry\, Turnpike Troubadours\, and Mountain Heart.
URL:https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/jam-cellars-presents-sierra-hull/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/SH_1200x800-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/paper-lanterns-workshop"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Paper Lanterns Workshop — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, Calif
 ornia
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260419T000000
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260420T000000
UID:0b2ea899ef80f7885f9155ba075c8bb1@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Paper Lanterns Workshop\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n       
    $70.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSunday\, April 19\, 2026\; 1:00PM
  – 4:00PM$60 + $10 Materials feeDiscover the magic of paper cutting In t
 his one-day workshop making your own paper lantern.  Participants will le
 arn paper cutting design and knife technique\, and create a unique\, illum
 inated piece of art. After exploring examples of paper cutting artists an
 d their work\, students will dream up their own paper lantern designs to e
 xecute with guidance and instruction. Learn how to translate your ideas in
 to a cut paper composition\, then how to cut out your composition with min
 imized frustration. Finally\, we will assemble our lanterns and illuminate
  them to bask in the glow of your efforts. This class will cover: proper 
 knife handling\, foundational paper cutting skills\, and the basics of pap
 er cutting design. A light box will be available if students would like to
  bring reference images to trace onto their lantern materials. This class
  is suitable for artists of all skill levels. All materials included\, inc
 luding an electric votive to illuminate your paper lantern safely. Safety 
 Note: Participants must have strong enough fine motor abilities to handle 
 a sharp blade safely. About the Instructor: Hannah Day received her BA in
  Visual Arts with an emphasis on drawing and printmaking from University o
 f San Diego\, then attended University of Hawaii at Manoa to receive her M
 FA in printmaking. Hannah’s etchings have been internationally shown and
  collected\, but her personal practice also includes paper cutting\, graph
 ite\, watercolor\, mixed media\, and murals. She has taught all ages and m
 any formats (kids\, teens\, adults\, college\, private lessons\, camps\, e
 tc) and many mediums. These days\, Hannah has primarily been teaching wate
 rcolor classes\, but also teaches drawing\, paper cutting\, and pop-up art
 . You can view her work at www.hannahdrawstrees.com\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        \n          \n         
    \n              Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/paper-lanterns-workshop
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
