X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Luther Burbank Center": "https://lutherburbankcenter.org/event/charley-crockett/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:luther_burbank_center
X-SOURCE:Luther Burbank Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T193000
DTSTAMP:20260317T222418
CREATED:20260317T130006Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260316T172053Z
UID:86236-1779651000-1779651000@lutherburbankcenter.org
SUMMARY:Charley Crockett - Age of the Ram Tour 🔑
DESCRIPTION:Back to All Shows\n\n\nCharley Crockett – Age of the Ram Tour with Special Guest Alicia Blue\n\nSunday\, May 24\, 2026\n\n7:30 pm\n\n\nBUY TICKETS \n🔑 Featuring a pre‑show Club for membership levels $500+. Click here for info. \n\n\nCharley Crockett has carved out a singular place in modern country music by refusing to play by the rules. A wanderer turned street singer turned chart-climbing songwriter\, he’s built a career on instinct\, independence\, and a deep reverence for the renegade tradition of artists like Willie Nelson\, Waylon Jennings\, and Gram Parsons. Fresh off the release of Age of the Ram\, the final chapter of his Sagebrush Trilogy\, Crockett arrives with a new batch of songs that paint a vivid picture of his journey from Texas dreamer\, New York street singer\, and twice-convicted felon to the belly of the country music beast. \nThis is Crockett’s vision of hard country music. Guitar and pedal steel are the rule on the album\, often accompanied by piano\, harmonica\, and keys. Produced by Shooter Jennings\, the record leans into hard country textures—guitar\, pedal steel\, harmonica\, and the dusty atmosphere of an old western film. Crockett threads narrative tracks\, character studies\, and classic covers into a vivid frontier tale\, punctuated by moments of introspection that reveal the man behind the myth. \n\nCharley Crockett\, in partnership with PLUS1\, will contribute $1.00 from every ticket sold to Last Prisoner Project\, a 501(c)(3) organization\, to support efforts to free individuals incarcerated for cannabis-related offenses and repair the harms of the war on cannabis. Founded in 2019\, Last Prisoner Project works nationwide to advance cannabis justice and advocate for policies that repair the harms of cannabis prohibition. Charley Crockett is proud to support this work and help raise awareness in communities across the country. For more information\, visit LastPrisonerProject.org. No portion of the ticket purchase is tax deductible.\n\n\n \n\nTHIRD PARTY RESELLERS\nDon’t get taken by deceptive online resellers who use bots to buy tickets and then mark up their prices. The only safe way to protect your purchase and guarantee the best seats at the lowest cost is to work directly with us: through our website\, by phone\, or at our box office in Santa Rosa. Plus\, we’re not bots. Our friendly team members are easily accessible by phone or at the box office to provide customer support.
URL:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/event/charley-crockett/
CATEGORIES:2025 - 2026 Season,Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CharleyCrocket26_SquareImageNOTEXT_1080x1080-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Uptowntheatrenapa": "https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/bottlerock-afterdark-maoli/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:uptowntheatrenapa
X-SOURCE:Uptowntheatrenapa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T220000
DTSTAMP:20260317T222428
CREATED:20260224T012007Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260224T181332Z
UID:25634-1779660000-1779660000@www.uptowntheatrenapa.com
SUMMARY:BOTTLEROCK AFTERDARK - Maoli
DESCRIPTION:May 24\, 2026\nPURCHASE TICKETS HERE  \nDoors 9pm/ Show 10pm\nAges: 12+ \nNow breaking into the mainstream with a unique mix of island reggae and country soul\, Hawaiian-born rising star Maoli seeks to put his people on the map like they’ve never been before. \nThe golden-voiced native of upcountry Maui boasts nine independent albums and over half a billion global streams\, with a nearly 15-year recording and touring career making him a fixture across the Pacific islands and beyond. Inspired by traditional Hawaiian music – the believe-it-or-not birthplace of steel guitar – plus rock\, reggae and the country music of artists like Dolly Parton\, Willie Nelson and George Strait\, Maoli’s early island pop and roots-reggae sound helped spread his rangy\, sand-and-soul vocal across Polynesia to the American West Coast\, and as far east as Texas. It was there in 2018 that the singer-songwriter rediscovered his country roots\, turned on to the similarities between his music and modern country – from the swaying melodies and solid rhythms to the tradition of simple-life storytelling. \nNow carrying the pride of his people across the globe\, his unique Hawaiian-country sound has driven a series of innovative albums and viral singles\, including emotionally-charged covers of hits like Brett Young’s “Mercy” (18+ million Spotify streams) and “In Case You Didn’t Know” (10+ million Spotify streams). \nNow\, Maoli has teamed up with hit producers Dann and David Huff to further bridge the gap between island soul and country tradition. The new album Last Sip of Summer (Island Vibe Edition is out now. \n 
URL:https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/event/bottlerock-afterdark-maoli/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.uptowntheatrenapa.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/BR26-Maoli-Uptown-Web-1200x800-1.png
END:VEVENT
